POLE: compliant (HookCharacterizationAnswer). Expected: the advisory ACCURATELY
describes the condition it fired on.

It names the two specific job keys, names the pool each targets, characterizes
the defect precisely as "consumes a runner slot on every pull request and cannot
block a merge", cites the clause it is enforcing, and states that the edit
stands. It is neither a generic style complaint nor a blocking error, and it
does not overstate — it says a job GATES NOTHING, not that the job is wrong.

